# qemu system user: libvirt runs guest processes as qemu:qemu
# (meson -Dqemu_user=qemu -Dqemu_group=qemu). Created at boot by
# systemd-sysusers.
#
# kvm membership is load-bearing: /dev/kvm ships 0660 root:kvm
# (systemd -Ddev-kvm-mode=0660) and the shipped kvm group has no
# members, so without this line qemu:qemu cannot open /dev/kvm and
# KVM-accelerated guests fail to start. Upstream's own fragment
# (src/qemu/libvirt-qemu.sysusers.conf, installed at this exact
# path) carries the same membership; this file replaces it and must
# not lose it.
u qemu - "QEMU guest process user" /var/lib/libvirt -
m qemu kvm
